# Arcade tests under `tests/`

## Shipping

Every project under `tests/` is non-shipping. Source of truth: `tests/Directory.Build.props`.

```xml
<Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />
<IsShipping>false</IsShipping>
<IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
<IsTestUtilityProject Condition="'$(IsUnitTestProject)' != 'true'">true</IsTestUtilityProject>
```

- **xUnit runners** — set `IsUnitTestProject=true` (required when the name does not end with `.Tests` / `.UnitTests`). Arcade then sets `IsTestProject` and runs `/t:Test`.
- **Harnesses** (AppHost, API, Data, MigrationService, ServiceDefaults) — `IsTestUtilityProject` from the directory props. Do **not** set `IsTestProject=true` globally (Arcade would look for an xUnit runner).

## SPA / JavaScript

- **Forbidden:** `.esproj`, `Microsoft.VisualStudio.JavaScript.Sdk`, listing a SPA in the `.slnx`.
- SPA is a Vite folder. Aspire wires it with `AddViteApp` on the path. No MSBuild project, no `ProjectReference` to the SPA.

## Nested `Directory.Build.*`

MSBuild uses the nearest file only. A nested `Directory.Build.props` / `.targets` **must import the parent**. An empty or dummy file (the old `.esproj` TFM/`Test`/`Pack` workaround) drops Arcade.

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<Project>
  <!-- Keep Arcade from stamping a TFM -->
</Project>
```

```xml
<!-- ✅ GOOD — only if a nested file is truly needed -->
<Project>
  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />
</Project>
```
